#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:1
msgid "jsprim: utilities for primitive JavaScript types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:3
msgid ""
"This module provides miscellaneous facilities for working with strings, "
"numbers, dates, and objects and arrays of these basic types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:7
msgid "deepCopy(obj)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:9
msgid ""
"Creates a deep copy of a primitive type, object, or array of primitive "
"types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:12
msgid "deepEqual(obj1, obj2)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:14
msgid "Returns whether two objects are equal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:17
msgid "isEmpty(obj)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:19
msgid ""
"Returns true if the given object has no properties and false otherwise.  "
"This is O(1) (unlike `Object.keys(obj).length === 0`, which is O(N))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:22
msgid "hasKey(obj, key)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:24
msgid ""
"Returns true if the given object has an enumerable, non-inherited "
"property called `key`.  [For information on enumerability and ownership "
"of properties, see the MDN documentation.](https://developer.mozilla.org"
"/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Enumerability_and_ownership_of_properties)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:29
msgid "forEachKey(obj, callback)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:31
msgid ""
"Like Array.forEach, but iterates enumerable, owned properties of an "
"object rather than elements of an array.  Equivalent to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:41
msgid "flattenObject(obj, depth)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:43
msgid ""
"Flattens an object up to a given level of nesting, returning an array of "
"arrays of length \"depth + 1\", where the first \"depth\" elements "
"correspond to flattened columns and the last element contains the "
"remaining object .  For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:80
msgid "becomes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:91
msgid ""
"This function is strict: \"depth\" must be a non-negative integer and "
"\"obj\" must be a non-null object with at least \"depth\" levels of "
"nesting under all keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:95
msgid "flattenIter(obj, depth, func)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:97
msgid ""
"This is similar to `flattenObject` except that instead of returning an "
"array, this function invokes `func(entry)` for each `entry` in the array "
"that `flattenObject` would return.  `flattenIter(obj, depth, func)` is "
"logically equivalent to `flattenObject(obj, depth).forEach(func)`.  "
"Importantly, this version never constructs the full array.  Its memory "
"usage is O(depth) rather than O(n) (where `n` is the number of flattened "
"elements)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:104
msgid ""
"There's another difference between `flattenObject` and `flattenIter` "
"that's related to the special case where `depth === 0`.  In this case, "
"`flattenObject` omits the array wrapping `obj` (which is regrettable)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:109
msgid "pluck(obj, key)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:111
msgid ""
"Fetch nested property \"key\" from object \"obj\", traversing objects as "
"needed. For example, `pluck(obj, \"foo.bar.baz\")` is roughly equivalent "
"to `obj.foo.bar.baz`, except that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:115
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"If traversal fails, the resulting value is undefined, and no error is "
"thrown.  For example, `pluck({}, \"foo.bar\")` is just undefined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:117
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"If \"obj\" has property \"key\" directly (without traversing), the "
"corresponding property is returned.  For example, `pluck({ 'foo.bar': 1 "
"}, 'foo.bar')` is 1, not undefined.  This is also true recursively, so "
"`pluck({ 'a': { 'foo.bar': 1 } }, 'a.foo.bar')` is also 1, not undefined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:124
msgid "randElt(array)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jsprim_README.md:126
msgid ""
"Returns an element from \"array\" selected uniformly at random.  If "
"\"array\" is empty, throws an Error."
msgstr ""

